+    /* IRIS_26625_RADIOMETRICALLY_VALIDATED_FALLBACK_GEOMETRY
+     * The direct-sun 26624 device trace proved a distinct false-closed case: SHORT was captured
+     * with 2.5 EV headroom, but only ~1% of sparse cells retained sub-pixel local-affine residuals,
+     * leaving zero boundary seeds. Build one deterministic frame-global affine hypothesis only from
+     * production-flow cells already inside the existing <=0.95 RAW-pixel strict residual envelope.
+     * RANSAC chooses the dominant sub-pixel model; spatial coverage and inlier residuals must pass.
+     * This model is geometry only. It cannot create component trust without the unchanged 5x5
+     * same-CFA NORMAL/SHORT boundary radiometry, and it is used for actual SHORT sampling only where
+     * that boundary-proven component trust exists.
